title: A stranger browsing 'docs/' would find the retired pages; 'orphaned/' and 'usage.org' would mislead, the two '-old' pages would not.
pid: cfe2b61e-4c1b-42cf-b2b4-050079cd2955
body: |2-
  Tay asked whether a stranger would find 'docs/orphaned/'. Yes: it
  and the two '-old' pages are in Git, so on any listing of the
  folder. 'README-old.org' calls itself "an early, flabby
  introduction", and 'OVERVIEW-old.org' "old overview": honest.
  'orphaned/public-mode.org' describes "public mode" in the present
  tense, as a feature, under a word the other pages do not use.
  'usage.org' says the same as 'setup.org' differently ('cargo run'
  against the start script), and names the same missing file.
  Change: fold 'usage.org' into 'setup.org' and delete it; move
  'orphaned/' and the '-old' pages out of 'docs/', once the essays
  are linked from 'docs/README.org'.
